<div class=3D"wrap">

<header class=3D"mast">
  <div class=3D"kicker">
    <span class=3D"eyebrow">Quiddity Innovations</span>
    <span class=3D"eyebrow">Design plan =C2=B7 per application</span>
    <span class=3D"eyebrow">5 September 2026</span>
  </div>
  <h1>Thirty-six apps, three tracks</h1>
  <p class=3D"standfirst">Every registered project scored on a fixed rubric=
, then a concrete plan for each one that earns work. Stacks were read from =
the code on your machine, not guessed =E2=80=94 and what the code says chan=
ges the answer.</p>
  <p class=3D"mono" style=3D"font-size:.78rem;color:var(--ink-3);">Revised =
=E2=80=94 Track B re-scored under the hybrid shell pattern. NEXUS 29 =E2=86=
=92 35, Quiddam 29 =E2=86=92 35, AkiyaScout 23 =E2=86=92 29.</p>
</header>

<section>
  <div class=3D"sec-head">
    <span class=3D"eyebrow">Correction first</span>
    <h2>Two things the audit got wrong</h2>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"panel crit">
    <p><strong style=3D"color:var(--ink)">NoosOrbis already has a full desi=
gn system.</strong> <span class=3D"mono">web/assets/app.css</span> is 798 l=
ines built on tokens, with a correctly structured three-state dark mode =E2=
=80=94 bare <span class=3D"mono">:root</span>, a <span class=3D"mono">prefe=
rs-color-scheme</span> block guarded against an explicit light choice, and =
a <span class=3D"mono">[data-theme=3D"dark"]</span> block. Type is Jost for=
 interface, Literata for reading, IBM Plex Mono for data. I saw the site in=
 light mode and wrote that it needed a dark mode. It has one, and it is bet=
ter built than most.</p>
    <p>That does not change the recommendation =E2=80=94 it makes it <em>mu=
ch</em> cheaper. The "one surface tone" problem is real but it is a <em>val=
ue-spacing</em> problem, not a missing-token problem: <span class=3D"mono">=
--ground #F1F3F7</span>, <span class=3D"mono">--surface #FFFFFF</span> and =
<span class=3D"mono">--surface-2 #E9EDF5</span> are too close together in l=
ight mode to read as three planes. That is three hex values, not an archite=
cture.</p>
    <p><strong style=3D"color:var(--ink)">And the design system I told you =
to extract from SynVox may not be the one to extract.</strong> NoosOrbis's =
token file is newer, simpler, dependency-free and already proves itself in =
both themes. SynVox's is Tailwind-bound. For a portfolio where most front e=
nds are plain HTML with no build step, NoosOrbis is the better donor.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class=3D"sec-head">
    <span class=3D"eyebrow">The structural finding</span>
    <h2>The Gradio ceiling</h2>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"prose" style=3D"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px=
;">
    <p>Reading the code turned up something more important than any individ=
ual app's styling. The QI project scaffold has a standard shape =E2=80=94 <=
span class=3D"mono">main.py</span>, <span class=3D"mono">ui/app.py</span>, =
<span class=3D"mono">requirements.txt</span> =E2=80=94 and in every case I =
checked, <span class=3D"mono">ui/app.py</span> imports Gradio.</p>
    <p>Gradio has a ceiling =E2=80=94 but a softer one than the first versi=
on of this document claimed. Gradio 5 has a real theming system (<span clas=
s=3D"mono">gr.themes.Base().set(...)</span> plus arbitrary <span class=3D"m=
ono">css=3D</span>), and NEXUS already uses it: <span class=3D"mono">ui/com=
mon.py</span> is 3,399 lines and ships <span class=3D"mono">NEXUS_THEME_CSS=
</span>, <span class=3D"mono">NEXUS_INIT_JS</span> and a working theme swit=
cher. Colour, type, radius and spacing <em>are</em> reachable.</p>
    <p>What is not reachable is the DOM: layout primitives, component inter=
nals, the page shell, navigation, and anything that needs a structure Gradi=
o does not already have. And every CSS override is written against markup t=
hat a version bump is free to change =E2=80=94 <span class=3D"mono">require=
ments.txt</span> pins <span class=3D"mono">gradio&gt;=3D5.0.0</span>, an op=
en floor.</p>
    <p><strong style=3D"color:var(--ink)">So the accurate statement is narr=
ower: Gradio is a good widget toolkit and a bad application shell.</strong>=
 Which means the fix is not to rebuild these apps =E2=80=94 it is to invert=
 the relationship, and make Gradio a component inside a shell you own. That=
 is the hybrid pattern, and it is set out in full below.</p>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"tbl-scroll">
    <table>
      <caption>The three tracks =E2=80=94 observed from the code</caption>
      <thead><tr><th>Track</th><th>Stack</th><th>Apps</th><th>What design w=
ork means here</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><span class=3D"pill p-a">Track A</span><br><strong>Own HTML</=
strong></td>
          <td>Hand-written <span class=3D"mono">index.html</span> + CSS + J=
S, no build step</td>
          <td>NoosOrbis =C2=B7 World Mythologies =C2=B7 Retirement Analyzer=
 <span class=3D"mono">web/</span> =C2=B7 PersonalSong =C2=B7 MediaStudio =
=C2=B7 VoiceStudio =C2=B7 AutoPDF =C2=B7 Gamez =C2=B7 Digitization Tool</td=
>
          <td>Adopt the shared tokens, fix spacing and hierarchy. Cheap, fa=
st, high return.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class=3D"pill p-b">Track B</span><br><strong>Gradio</st=
rong></td>
          <td><span class=3D"mono">ui/app.py</span> importing <span class=
=3D"mono">gradio</span></td>
          <td>NEXUS =C2=B7 AkiyaScout =C2=B7 TubeScout =C2=B7 MQ =C2=B7 M2V=
 =C2=B7 AvatarStudio =C2=B7 CypherMiner <span class=3D"mono">ui/</span> =C2=
=B7 Retirement Analyzer <span class=3D"mono">ui/</span></td>
          <td>Cannot be polished. Each one needs an explicit decision: rebu=
ild the front end, or accept it as an internal tool forever.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class=3D"pill p-c">Track C</span><br><strong>No surface=
</strong></td>
          <td>Services, MCP servers, libraries, meta-workspaces</td>
          <td>QI Brain =C2=B7 QI Connector =C2=B7 Headroom =C2=B7 OpenClaw =
=C2=B7 Claude Manager =C2=B7 CogniBase =C2=B7 FilmForge =C2=B7 EasyFlow =C2=
=B7 OnBase DNA =C2=B7 FileHQ =C2=B7 QI-Universal =C2=B7 ComfyUI</td>
          <td>Nothing to design. Two of them are worth designing <em>before=
</em> they get a surface.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"callout">Two apps already broke out of Track B on their own=
: CypherMiner has a Vite + TypeScript PWA front end sitting beside its Grad=
io <span class=3D"mono">ui/</span>, and the Retirement Analyzer has a vanil=
la <span class=3D"mono">web/</span> folder beside its. The migration patter=
n you need already exists in your own repos, twice.</div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class=3D"sec-head">
    <span class=3D"eyebrow">The method for Track B</span>
    <h2>One application, two technologies</h2>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"prose" style=3D"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px=
;">
    <p>The user never needs to know where a page comes from. A shell you co=
ntrol owns the identity, the navigation and every page that carries the pro=
duct's impression; Gradio keeps the panels where it is genuinely good =E2=
=80=94 queued jobs, streaming output, progress, file handling =E2=80=94 and=
 is embedded inside that shell. One URL, one visual system, two technologie=
s.</p>
    <p>Reading the NEXUS code settled whether this is cheap or expensive, a=
nd the answer is decisive.</p>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"panel">
    <span class=3D"eyebrow">The finding that changes the plan</span>
    <p><span class=3D"mono">ui/common.py</span> line 18: <span class=3D"mon=
o">API_BASE =3D "http://127.0.0.1:8010"</span>. Every NEXUS tab reaches its=
 functionality through <span class=3D"mono">httpx.get / post / delete / str=
eam</span> against that address. <strong style=3D"color:var(--ink)">The Gra=
dio UI is already nothing but an HTTP client of your own REST API.</strong>=
 No business logic lives in the UI layer. There is nothing entangled to unp=
ick.</p>
    <p>That means replacing a Gradio surface is not a rewrite. It is writin=
g a new client for an API that already exists, is already routed (<span cla=
ss=3D"mono">api/routers/</span>: batch, bench, config, core, personas, rag,=
 scout) and already streams (<span class=3D"mono">/synthesize/stream</span>=
). The audit's "5=E2=80=936 session rewrite, high stall risk" estimate for =
NEXUS was wrong, and this is why.</p>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"tbl-scroll">
    <table>
      <caption>The split =E2=80=94 who owns what</caption>
      <thead><tr><th>Surface</th><th>Owner</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Front page, navigation, identity, auth, settings, d=
ashboards, reading views</strong></td><td><span class=3D"pill p-a">Your she=
ll</span></td><td>These carry the entire impression and Gradio is worst at =
exactly these. They are also the easiest to build =E2=80=94 mostly static p=
ages against a JSON API.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Long-running jobs, queued dispatch, streaming outpu=
t, progress bars, file upload, ad-hoc admin forms</strong></td><td><span cl=
ass=3D"pill p-b">Gradio panel</span></td><td>Gradio gives you queueing, str=
eaming, progress and file handling for free. Rebuilding that is weeks of wo=
rk for no visible gain.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Anything a stranger sees first</strong></td><td><sp=
an class=3D"pill p-a">Your shell</span></td><td>Non-negotiable. The rule fo=
r the scaffold: Gradio is allowed anywhere except <span class=3D"mono">/</s=
pan>.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"prose" style=3D"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px=
;">
    <h3>How it is wired</h3>
    <p>One process, one port, one origin. <span class=3D"mono">gr.mount_gra=
dio_app(app, blocks, path=3D"/panel/orchestrator")</span> mounts each Gradi=
o surface onto the same FastAPI app that serves the shell. Same origin matt=
ers more than it sounds: it means one cookie jar, one tunnel, no CORS, and =
=E2=80=94 because the parent page can reach into a same-origin iframe's doc=
ument directly =E2=80=94 height sync and theme injection become a few lines=
 instead of a postMessage protocol.</p>
    <p><strong style=3D"color:var(--ink)">The detail that makes the seam in=
visible:</strong> generate the Gradio theme <em>from</em> <span class=3D"mo=
no">qi-tokens.css</span> at startup. A small <span class=3D"mono">qi_gradio=
_theme.py</span> reads the token file and returns a configured <span class=
=3D"mono">gr.themes.Base()</span>, so both halves of the app derive their c=
olour, radius and type from one source. Change a token, both sides move. Wi=
thout this, you maintain two palettes and they drift within a month.</p>
    <p>Then strangle it. NEXUS has nine independent tabs in <span class=3D"=
mono">ui/tabs/</span>. Each one is a separate, replaceable unit. Replace th=
e ones that carry impression =E2=80=94 Orchestrator, Hub, Scout =E2=80=94 a=
nd leave Settings and Bench in Gradio indefinitely. The iframe disappears o=
ne route at a time, and the work is stoppable at any point without leaving =
anything half-built.</p>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"panel gold">
    <span class=3D"eyebrow">What this costs =E2=80=94 the honest side</span=
>
    <p>You now own the seam, and the seam is not free:</p>
    <ul class=3D"tight">
      <li><strong>Bundle weight.</strong> Gradio ships a large JS payload. =
Your shell loads instantly, the panel does not, and users read that gap as =
"the app is slow" =E2=80=94 even though the slow part is the part you did n=
ot write. Prefetch the panel, or accept a visible skeleton.</li>
      <li><strong>Version pin.</strong> <span class=3D"mono">gradio&gt;=3D5=
.0.0</span> must become <span class=3D"mono">=3D=3D</span>. Every CSS overr=
ide and every height assumption is written against markup Gradio is free to=
 change in a minor release.</li>
      <li><strong>Height and scroll.</strong> An embedded panel needs its h=
eight synced or you get a scrollbar inside a scrollbar. Same-origin makes t=
his tractable; it still needs writing once, in the shared shell script, not=
 per app.</li>
      <li><strong>Back button and deep links.</strong> Navigation inside a =
panel does not move browser history. Decide early whether panels get real U=
RLs.</li>
      <li><strong>Mobile.</strong> Gradio inside a constrained frame degrad=
es badly. If mobile matters for a given app, that panel is the first to go =
native.</li>
      <li><strong>Two mental models.</strong> Six months from now you will =
have to remember which half a given page lives in.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong style=3D"color:var(--ink)">Which is why this is not a portfo=
lio-wide answer.</strong> For an app with an audience of one, the seam cost=
s more than the ugliness it hides. TubeScout, M2V and AvatarStudio stay pla=
in Gradio =E2=80=94 not because the pattern would not work, but because nob=
ody is looking.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class=3D"sec-head">
    <span class=3D"eyebrow">Method</span>
    <h2>How each app was scored</h2>
  </div>
  <div class=3D"prose"><p>Four factors, each 0=E2=80=935, weighted so that =
reach and ease dominate =E2=80=94 because you are one person and the only t=
hing that converts design effort into value is somebody seeing it.</p></div=
>
