        <span class=3D"fact"><b>Tabs</b> 9 independent modules in ui/tabs/<=
/span>
        <span class=3D"fact"><b>Effort</b> 1 session shell + ~0.5 per tab</=
span>
      </div>
      <p>Multi-provider parallel dispatch with chain and iterative refineme=
nt modes is the most impressive thing in the portfolio, and it is presented=
 in Gradio's default orange. Widest gap in QI between what something <em>is=
</em> and what it looks like.</p>
      <p><strong style=3D"color:var(--ink)">Re-scored from 29 to 35.</stron=
g> The audit called this a 5=E2=80=936 session rewrite with high stall risk=
. The code says otherwise: the UI holds no logic, every tab talks to <span =
class=3D"mono">:8010</span> over HTTP, and the nine tabs are already separa=
te modules. This is not a rewrite =E2=80=94 it is a shell plus a queue of i=
ndependent, individually shippable tab replacements.</p>
      <h4 style=3D"color:var(--ink);font-family:Inter,sans-serif;font-weigh=
t:600;margin-top:4px;">Session 1 =E2=80=94 the shell</h4>
      <ol class=3D"steps">
        <li>Pin <span class=3D"mono">gradio=3D=3D</span> the version you ar=
e on. Do this before anything else; every step below writes against Gradio'=
s markup.</li>
        <li>Serve a static shell at <span class=3D"mono">/</span> from the =
same FastAPI app, importing <span class=3D"mono">qi-tokens.css</span>. It o=
wns the masthead, the nav, and the provider/economics summary =E2=80=94 all=
 of which are plain reads from the existing API.</li>
        <li><span class=3D"mono">gr.mount_gradio_app()</span> each existing=
 tab at <span class=3D"mono">/panel/&lt;name&gt;</span> on that same app. S=
ame origin, one port, one tunnel.</li>
        <li>Write <span class=3D"mono">qi_gradio_theme.py</span>: parse <sp=
an class=3D"mono">qi-tokens.css</span>, return a configured <span class=3D"=
mono">gr.themes.Base()</span>. One palette, both halves.</li>
        <li>Write the height-sync and theme-propagation code once, in the s=
hared shell script =E2=80=94 not per app. Same origin makes it short.</li>
      </ol>
      <h4 style=3D"color:var(--ink);font-family:Inter,sans-serif;font-weigh=
t:600;">Then, one tab at a time =E2=80=94 stop whenever you like</h4>
      <ol class=3D"steps" start=3D"6">
        <li><strong>Orchestrator first.</strong> It is the landing tab and =
the whole product story. Providers as a live roster with per-provider state=
, routing mode as three real options, dispatch as the moment the screen is =
built around. <span class=3D"mono">/synthesize/stream</span> already exists=
, so streaming works from day one.</li>
        <li><strong>Hub second</strong> =E2=80=94 spend and usage are numbe=
rs, and numbers are where a custom front end wins hardest. This is where th=
e "levers" idea earns its keep: a provider-selection change recomputes cost=
 and latency locally and springs to the new figures with no round trip.</li=
>
        <li><strong>Scout third.</strong> A digest is a reading surface; Gr=
adio is poor at reading surfaces.</li>
        <li><strong>Leave Settings, Bench, Batch, Curate, Personas and Help=
 in Gradio.</strong> They are forms and tables for an audience of one. Repl=
acing them buys nothing.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class=3D"donewhen"><b>Done when:</b> the three impression-carryi=
ng tabs are native, the rest are embedded panels that match them in colour =
and type, and a visitor cannot tell which is which without opening dev tool=
s.</div>
      <div class=3D"risk"><b>Risk:</b> far lower than the rewrite it replac=
es =E2=80=94 every step ships something usable =E2=80=94 but the panel bund=
le is heavy, so the shell will feel instant and the panels will not. Prefet=
ch, or show a real skeleton rather than a spinner.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D 05 MQ =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
