    </div>
    <div class=3D"scorestrip">
      <div><span class=3D"k">Reach</span><span class=3D"v">4<small>apex dom=
ain</small></span></div>
      <div><span class=3D"k">Gap</span><span class=3D"v">4<small>inferred</=
small></span></div>
      <div><span class=3D"k">Strategic</span><span class=3D"v">3</span></di=
v>
      <div><span class=3D"k">Ease</span><span class=3D"v">3<small>was 1 =E2=
=80=94 shell pattern</small></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"body">
      <div class=3D"facts">
        <span class=3D"fact"><b>Stack</b> Gradio (ui/app.py)</span>
        <span class=3D"fact"><b>Public</b> quiddam.com =E2=80=94 apex, curr=
ently sign-in walled</span>
        <span class=3D"fact"><b>Effort</b> 1 session, once one question is =
answered</span>
      </div>
      <p><strong style=3D"color:var(--ink)">This is a decision, not a task.=
</strong> Quiddam is your apex public domain and it is a Gradio app behind =
a sign-in wall. Those two facts are incompatible with each other.</p>
      <p>The shell pattern collapses the decision, though. You no longer ha=
ve to choose between "public front door" and "internal Gradio console" =E2=
=80=94 the apex serves a real public page, and the console stays exactly as=
 it is at <span class=3D"mono">/panel/console</span>, behind auth. That is =
the single clearest case for the hybrid in the whole portfolio: the two aud=
iences want genuinely different things from the same hostname.</p>
      <ul class=3D"tight">
        <li>If quiddam.com should greet strangers: one static page at <span=
 class=3D"mono">/</span> =E2=80=94 what Maia Quiddam is, what it posts, a l=
ive sample of the combined feed. One session, no rewrite of anything behind=
 it.</li>
        <li>If it is purely an internal console: leave it, drop Reach to 1,=
 and it joins the "leave it" bucket with TubeScout.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class=3D"donewhen"><b>Done when:</b> you have answered which of =
those two it is. I could not determine it from behind the sign-in screen.</=
div>
